I just, I kind of forget that that exists.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.900
That's still a thing.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:48.940
1988, here we are and Captain Commando, who hasn't even had his own game yet on the system, is just basically Capcom's mascot at this point.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.900
But I'd argue almost any other Capcom game that's come out could have been their mascot instead.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.140
It's like that whole like, why do you keep trying to make Captain Commando a thing?

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.600
It's never going to be a thing.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.880
I don't understand it.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.480
I'm waiting for a Captain Commando reboot.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.900
Yeah? Yeah. We refresh our memory.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.740
What is the Captain Commando challenge?

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.560
Well, the Captain Commando challenge is just beat the game, kind of.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:17.340
You know, and it's like, if you look in the manual, it's always like a special message from Captain Commando.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.000
And this is for all of the games that have that.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.900
And it's just like, thanking you for buying the game.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:29.360
And then just like, you know, one of the, it's part of the Captain Commando challenge series.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.140
Right. So it's not a challenge to complete, compete all of those games.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.240
Like, once you beat all the games, you've completed.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.200
You get a t-shirt.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.380
Yeah, you've completed the Captain Commando challenge.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.260
I like the idea better.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:48.820
It's like Mega Man, where like, you actually have to beat all of these games first, and then you send in the beating games, and then you unlock Captain Commando.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:54.600
Yeah. You know? I think they ship you a game that's like the final level with all of the games incorporated in some way.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.180
Yeah. And actually, now that we were talking about Mega Man, Captain Commando wasn't part of that.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.400
Right? Mega Man was just his own thing.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.300
It wasn't like part of the Captain Commando challenge.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.940
I think that maybe like Captain Commando is just Mega Man in disguise.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:14.240
Okay. He's more like Cable from, not Cable TV, Cable from like Marvel.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.260
Like X-Men Cable?

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.240
Yeah, X-Men Cable.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:22.240
He looks a lot like that, except for, from what I can best tell, he just wields guns on both hands.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.240
Like, he has no hands, he just has guns for hands.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.980
I dig it. I like it too.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:35.440
One thing also we should note is that I called this game Gun Smoke, but there is a dot or a period in there.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.640
So we didn't call it Gun.Smoke.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.200
I didn't think of it like the .hack series on the PS2.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:51.020
I can't tell if we should like refer to it as like, like DRIV3R for Driver 3 or like all these weird like stylizations of names.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.420
I didn't realize that it started so, so early.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.520
Mm-hmm. I feel like, I feel like DRIV3R is ridiculous.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.520
I love DRIV3R though.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.660
Like that's very clear to me what it should and shouldn't be.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.040
You know, like, that would be like saying, is it 007?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.480
You remember DRIV3R though, right?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.840
I'm just saying like, is it 007 or is it ooze?

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.480
Like... No one says it.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.980
Those are the letters. Seven gets the, it's like four being the letter A.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.060
Like, could it decide these things?

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.980
But it could be, is it 007 or is it just seven?

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.140
Right, oh yeah, yeah, yeah. Because you don't pronounce the two O's before.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.080
Yeah, in fact, there's actually an infinite amount of zeros in front of any number.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.280
Right, yeah. That's important to remember.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.440
Oh, excited. Is that true for even like things that have zeros after it?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.500
Yeah. So if it's like a million, there's still like millions of zeros in front of them?

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.360
I mean, you know, mathematics is just a concept.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.260
So, I mean, if it virtually has zeros in front of it, then it doesn't matter.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:44.920
I boomed ya.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.320
Okay, cool. You boomed me and now I'm going to boom you with a fact.

