But before we get into gameplay, we should do a little Tales from the manual.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:23.780
The only, the only thing I really wanted to mention outside of the plot, which I think we should get into because that's always fun, is just like the level of detail that has gone into this manual to give you like a level of awareness of what you're doing in a game that doesn't tell you much.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:33.000
Like, you get the names of all of the enemy bosses, you get the names of the like locations for each stage, you get the names of every single enemy.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:39.380
I just, I like this level of comprehensiveness that we usually only see in like Nintendo NES manuals.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.780
Right. And it's funny because before this podcast, it seemed like that's just a given.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.180
Put that stuff in the manual.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.760
Right. That you should just, that stuff, information should be available somewhere.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.220
So it's weird that it doesn't show up more often.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.460
Yeah. And I even like the art too of like the wanted posters.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:56.900
Yeah, the wanted posters are cool.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:02.860
Um, I, I think that it's not even close to being like our most like ludicrous manual.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:11.400
Oh no, I still think that kind of goes to like Legend of Zelda for just like really covering like how to do most of the beginning of the game and like having a.

