00:55:23.480 --> 00:56:15.300
Mhm. When we started the episode, we mentioned the 1942 and Commando connection.

00:56:16.280 --> 00:56:32.780
I'm just wondering how you guys feel about the on-rails approach that Gunsmoke took versus the Commando approach where you got to freely walk around in the same similar kind of layout.

00:56:32.780 --> 00:56:37.540
Would you have preferred to be able to just navigate yourself through this Wild West?

00:56:37.540 --> 00:56:51.740
I found that because I was not a fan of Commando in any regard, that the fact that you were just sort of shooting out the front of you at all times was what really did that game in for me.

00:56:52.100 --> 00:57:04.220
And I think that because there's no way to strafe in that game, if you were to be able to freely walk around, it would basically end up being just like Commando.

00:57:04.220 --> 00:57:19.760
Whereas with this just slowly walking you forward, you can treat it as like just another space shmup, at least in the feel of the controls and allow you to be a lot more maneuverable in yourself.

00:57:19.920 --> 00:57:22.940
I really hated the feel of Commando.

00:57:22.940 --> 00:57:27.260
And if this was just walk yourself, it would feel just like that.

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:34.200
I didn't hate Commando, but if you were to ask me that question before I had played either of these games, I would have said I would like to freely move around.

00:57:34.780 --> 00:57:40.640
But there's definitely other factors into why I liked this game so much more than Commando.

00:57:40.860 --> 00:57:42.200
But that's one of them.

00:57:42.280 --> 00:57:43.300
I think it's one of those things.

00:57:43.440 --> 00:57:49.600
We talked about it in the Punch-Out episode where it doesn't need to give you control over things that you don't need control over.

00:57:49.820 --> 00:57:52.480
And I think that's part of what makes this game good.

00:57:52.480 --> 00:57:54.340
You're focused on killing everyone.

00:57:54.440 --> 00:57:56.140
You're not focused on where am I going next.

00:57:56.140 --> 00:57:58.000
Yeah. And that's what this game is about.

00:57:58.080 --> 00:58:00.200
I agree. It's about focusing on that stuff.

